Is this regarding "NetHack" or "bones level issues" (I'm not aware of
any big problem with bones).

In NetHack there are to this day bugs discovered, some even not listed
on the "official" bug list of the DevTeam.
http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Bugs_in_NetHack_3.4.3#Bugs_not_mentioned_on_the_DevTeam.27s_website

A new bones bug would not be an unthinkable discovery.

> True, and official patches would be welcome.

Yes but patches shouldn't only be sent to the DevTeam. They currently
act as a black hole for bug reports and patches. The most likely
response will be "doesn't apply cleanly, our dev version has diverged
too much from 3.4.3 already".

Send them to one of the active fork developers or the admin of
nethack.alt.org. We make sure that the word about new bugs reaches the
people that should now about it.

> But the bugs are well
> known by now, since so many man-hours have been spent playing vanilla
> 3.4.3. And happily they occur rarely, at least on the platform where
> I'm playing.

This has more to do with your way of playing or even of most players'
way. There are still code paths that are taken quite rarely and bugs
are discovered every year.

Otherwise it wouldn't have taken almost 10 years until the "Book of
the Dead gets destroyed when player falls into lava" or the "crash
while restoring when riding and wielding Sting" bugs have been
discovered.

I wasn't surprised that we'd see new bugs being discovered as I have
quite an intimate knowledge the code. But I was still surprised that
bugs of this severity where still lurking in there.

